NV_PK(36,{"hinoki needs about 300 years to grow one cubic meter of wood so its wood is pricier":"","spicy scent":"","hinoki wood is rich in oil and has a spicy scent red cypress smells sweet and is not spicy":"","cloud forest belt":"","both grow in the mid elevation mountains about 1 500 to 2 500 meters often mixed together":"","taiwan cypress":"","because they grow together the two trees are often jointly called 'taiwan cypress'":"","alishan qilan and lalashan":"","the best places to see taiwan's cypress trees there is more hinoki in the north and more red cypress in the south":"","red cypress leaves feel prickly when you stroke them backwards":"","hinoki cones are shaped like eggs":"","most sacred giant trees are red cypress":"","hinoki grows faster than red cypress":"","red cypress is nicknamed 'thin skin'":""});